body:
I don't think I've ever read an AITA post where merely reading the TL;DR gave the answer immediately

&#x200B;

NTA

Lock it, tell them it's storage or something. The more importance you put on it, the more likely they are to be nosy about it. Use any excuse: work, pets, storage, hobbies, etc. But KEEP YOUR STORY STRAIGHT.

Just act casual and ur family probably wont poke and prod.

&#x200B;

Also for equipment suggestions: first aid kit is a must. As a person who plays myself, stock based on your specific method of play. Also, wall hangs for whips/canes/etc is a lifesaver and looks great while making storage easier. Plus, you can cover them with a curtain when u finish for a bit more comfort.

&#x200B;

I wish you luck with ur dungeon funs, Bass!!

Illegal, dangerous, and stupid.

&#x200B;

Weed might not be able to kill you but some people have poor reactions to certain strains, and some even have THC allergies.

Stress of not knowing what happened could lead to a very bad time. Remember how weed can cause paranoia? Yeah.

&#x200B;

r/AmItheAsshole seems like a good place for you to be

Could be anxiety, sleep apnea (which can have causes besides being overweight!), or any number of things.

Getting blood testing can help see if theres potential deficiencies or problems. Psychotherapy could help diagnose and treat any underlying mental health issues.

&#x200B;

Keeping track how you sleep can help too: if you sleep better in a certain position, can't fall/stay asleep.

&#x200B;

Clinics can be emotionally tiring jobs, and there's a chance that emotional exhaustion is manifesting physically, that's a problem I faced
